+"The async logger implementation is fantastic. The log trace is exactly what we need. However, before we move to the next feature, please apply one quick fix to the logger:
+
+Quick Fix: In logger.cpp, change basic_file_sink_mt to rotating_file_sink_mt (include <spdlog/sinks/rotating_file_sink.h>). Set it to rotate at 10 MB with a maximum of 5 files. This prevents the disk from filling up during 24/7 live execution.
+
+Once the logger fix is applied, immediately move on to Task 3: Harden the TimeOfDayFilter (Trading Hours).
+
+    Ensure TimeOfDayFilter in filter.hpp handles local time conversions correctly based on the timestamp in the MarketContext.
+
+    Ensure it supports overnight sessions (e.g., if a user sets start_h = 22 and end_h = 02, it should correctly allow trades crossing midnight).
+
+    Add an spdlog::trace (using our new LOG_TRACE macro) when the TimeOfDayFilter rejects a trade, so we can see it in the audit log."

